## Copies of the passwords on the servers {#security-copies}

The servers hold copies of the passwords, readable by root only:

{% if f.backup.enabled %}
- `/opt/ansibro/backup/installer/state/secrets/` on {{ f.first_manager }}: **every password**, refreshed on each install, and inside every backup of {{ f.first_manager }}.
- `/opt/ansibro/backup/password` on every server: the backup password.
{% endif %}
- `.env` files in `/opt/ansibro/<app>/` of the apps that use them.
{% if has("portainer") %}
- `/opt/ansibro/portainer/admin_password`.
{% endif %}
{% if has("authelia") %}
- `/opt/ansibro/authelia/config/` (configuration, users and notifications).
{% endif %}
- `/root/.docker/config.json` (the registry login).

So anyone with root on {{ f.first_manager }}{% if f.backup.enabled %}, or with the backup password and storage{% endif %}, has every password.
On the installer computer, `state/` is {% if f.state == "age" %}**encrypted** (state.age){% elif f.state == "plain" %}**not encrypted**. Recommended: turn on ansibro's encryption (age){% else %}not present{% endif %}.

## SSH keys {#security-ssh}

An *SSH key* is a pair of files that lets a person log in without a password. ansibro does not add or remove SSH keys. Who may log in is the list in `~/.ssh/authorized_keys` of `{{ f.ssh.user }}` on each server; keep it short and remove keys of people who leave.

